== Biography ==

Robert Glasgow is named as a father in Libberton, Lanarkshire, parish baptism entries from 1718 to 1726:

* [[Glasgow-4130|Janet Glasgow]], baptised 22 April 1718, with mother [[Gibson-37713|Katherin Gibson]];<ref name="Janet1718">Findmypast, ''Scotland, Parish Births & Baptisms 1564–1929'', Libberton Old Parish Register, [https://www.findmypast.co.uk/transcript?id=SCOT%2FOPR%2FBAP%2F4033250&tab=this Janet Glasgow, 22 April 1718]. The child profile retains the full index citation.</ref>
* [[Glasgow-4133|Agnes Glasgow]], baptised 21 August 1720, with mother Katherine Wilson;<ref name="Agnes1720">Findmypast, ''Scotland, Parish Births & Baptisms 1564–1929'', Libberton Old Parish Register, [https://www.findmypast.co.uk/transcript?id=SCOT%2FOPR%2FBAP%2F4033335&tab=this Agnes Glasgow, 21 August 1720].</ref>
* [[Glasgow-4107|Elizabeth Glasgow]], baptised 10 June 1726, with mother Katherine Watson.<ref name="Elizabeth1726">Findmypast, ''Scotland, Parish Births & Baptisms 1564–1929'', Libberton Old Parish Register; the full entry is cited on [[Glasgow-4107]].</ref>

No birth, baptism or death record for this adult Robert has been identified. Birth before about 1699 is an age estimate based on the first child; Libberton is a recorded household parish, not a proved birthplace.

== Research Notes ==
=== Agnes’s recorded mother — 22 October 2026 ===

Agnes’s 21 August 1720 entry records Katherine Wilson, not Watson. The detailed transcript was reinspected: OPR 650/1, item 3, p.11, residence Gladhaimb; no birth date/year or sex field. Two further index versions give Katharin Wilson, indexed birth year 1720 and sex Female.<ref>Findmypast, ''Scotland, Parish Births & Baptisms 1564-1929'', [https://www.findmypast.co.uk/transcript?id=SCOT%2FOPR%2FBAP%2F4033335&tab=this SCOT/OPR/BAP/4033335], [https://www.findmypast.co.uk/transcript?id=R_684955704&tab=this R_684955704] and [https://www.findmypast.co.uk/transcript?id=R_693522269&tab=this R_693522269], inspected 22 October 2026; duplicate versions of the Libberton baptism. Original register uninspected.</ref> Whether [[Watson-53558|Katherine Watson]] represents the woman indexed as Wilson remains unresolved. Agnes’s live mother field was 0 at this review. Existing wife links, Elizabeth’s separate 1726 mother reading and the uncertain father model are retained; no mother or wife is attached, detached, renamed or created.


The former Glasgow-4169 profile represented the Robert named with Katherin Gibson in 1718. It was merged into this Robert-and-Katherine-Watson profile on 27 September 2026. The same father name and parish across the entries, with no distinct same-name adult identified, support treating them as one man. The maternal surnames differ. They may represent two women, a remarriage, or a register/transcription discrepancy. Existing wife links and all three child entries remain recorded; the indexed Wilson surname does not establish another woman, and no marriage, death or surname change is asserted without further evidence.

Compare the original 1718, 1720 and 1726 register pages, then search Libberton marriages and burials for Katherin Gibson and Katherine Wilson/Watson, without treating the last two surnames as an established identity.

